    "scale_id": 36415,
    "comment": "\r\nIn ex00, he demonstrated a solid understanding of constructor and destructor behavior in derived classes, ensuring the expected hierarchy in print messages.\r\n\r\nFor ex01, I loved his creative approach with \"brainwash\" (deep copy with a new address) and \"mindreading\" (regular copy). Instead of adding the brain class to the animal, he placed it in the derived class, adding fun features like thoughts and distractions. He explained virtual functionality well and even created dialogues within the brain class, adding detailed and entertaining interactions.\r\n\r\nIn ex02, he gave a clear, simple explanation of abstract classes and the =0 for virtual functions.\r\n\r\nIn ex03, he noted some issues in the assignment itself, like a non-pure constructor affecting pure functions. He created a simple garbage collector in the unequip function to delete items when the maximum was reached.\r\n\r\nOverall, his work was creative, detailed, and showed a great understanding of each task. Great job, and thank you for your time!",
